  "live_records": {
    "q-318127": {
      "dom_id": "step-q318127",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "What number is $125%$ greater than $64?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find a number $125%$ *greater than* $64,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+125%=225%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n225%=\\frac{225}{100}=2.25\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $125%$ greater than $64,$ we multiply $64$ by $2.25:$\n\n$$\n2.25\\cdot 64=144\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number that is $125%$ greater than $64$ is $144.$",
