    "q-327654": {
      "dom_id": "step-q327654",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "A factory produced $900$ boxes of cereal last year. This year, production is $300%$ greater than last year. How many boxes of cereal did the factory produce this year?\n\nThe factory produced\n{{field-1}}\nboxes of cereal this year.",
      "worked_solution": "To find this year's cereal production, we apply a $300%$ increase to last year's figure.\n\nIncreasing by $300%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+300%=400%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n400%=\\frac{400}{100}=4\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original amount by $4:$\n\n$$\n900\\times 4=3,600\n$$\n\nSo, the factory produced $3600$ boxes of cereal this year.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
